{"id":"par","lemma":"par","pos":"noun","rank":356,"glosses":["pair (two of the same or similar items that go together)","couple (two of the same or similar items)","two equal non-collinear forces; that is a force couple in Newtonian mechanics"],"ipa":"/ˈpaɾ/","gender":"m","forms":{"plural":"pares"},"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-AdrianAbdulBaha-par.wav","examples":[{"text":"Es un número par.","en":"It's an even number.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/541241"},{"text":"Por favor, no pares.","en":"Please don't stop.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/164742"},{"text":"Dame un par de días.","en":"Give me a couple days.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/851440"},{"text":"Será mejor que pares.","en":"You'd better leave it.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/459284"},{"text":"Tengo un par de zapatos.","en":"I have a pair of shoes.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/458986"}]}